From c4565ec4d7282370c40afbe690839ed22051e626 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:49:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tui): trusted durable producer completion ingress for
 unrouted inline sessions [daveey]

An inline TUI/Desktop chat with no gateway route or local receipt had no durable ingress for a
producer completion (a finished user-terminal job): admit_automation needs a route, adoption
needs an authenticated native transport and refuses a live inline owner, and plugin_inject makes
ordinary user input.

hermes_state_producer_admission.admit_producer_completion(producer, profile_home,
stored_session_id, text) records one row per producer identity in the profile's own store
(admitted queued|committed|dispatched, routed, missing, retry; same producer + different payload
raises). Only the owning inline runtime delivers it, through the existing notice channel: the
chat's poller claims the idle turn, refuses another owner (no takeover), writes one
process_complete notice on the compression tip and marks it committed in one txn, then runs it as
a synthesized turn adopting that row, with no @-reference expansion. A refused dispatch re-stages
the same row; a turn that already ran is not rerun. A Desktop/serve sweeper wakes cold chats via
in-process session.resume and honors ownership refusals. A session adopted after admission is
retired as routed, never delivered here.
